  m_md_role_wanted: ["TASK_KINDS is only an enum. Kind feeds the model-pick judgment (writer-model-pick.ts:54) and the lane queue (start.ts:801). Nothing narrows the worker pool to those holding a named role."],
  m_mo_estimate: ["tokenDelta is per-turn delta arithmetic. No estimate is made when the vendor is silent; attempt metrics only label costState measured/partial/not_measured."],
  m_mo_fallback: ["A paid lane is allowed while under the cap, but nothing ties it to all subscription windows being closed; routing is by chain order. No windows-closed-then-money transition."],
  m_mo_rule: ["moneyHold holds a paid lane once spend reaches the cap. With no cap it does not hold, so paid lanes run unlimited (card: only when the cap is set). 'Only when all windows are closed' is not enforced here."],
  m_mo_series: ["series covers 14 days but is per day only (day, usd). The per-account split (byProvider) is for the month total, not per day."],
  m_mo_stop: ["Stop is in moneyHold (capOf is just the parser): a paid lane holds when spend >= cap. Missing: the 'task would exceed the cap' case."],
  m_mo_task_ceiling: ["overBudget stops a running writer past its task appetite (minutes/tokens) or the run budget. It is not a pre-start check against the monthly money remainder."],
  m_mo_unset: ["deliberate: an unset monthly cap means no limit — every lane the owner runs is a subscription (2026-11-10); the card reads an unset cap as zero for paid lanes"],
  m_not_green: ["status lists held provider/model keys (pool.held) without a reason; check() is the harness-fault canary alert. No per-worker reason, no recorded refusal of its tasks."],
  m_out_lift_failed: ["Second message 'не поднялся после N попыток' is sent once per exhausted lift sequence, but the text is fixed; no reason taken from the lift's own output."],
  m_out_marker: ["lane_pilot_outage stores only from_at (last beat), to_at, minutes, cause, noticed_at (plugin heartbeat gap). Declaration, messages and lift attempts are not in it; only outage/lift events sit in the watchdog's outages.jsonl, no messages."],
  m_out_notify: ["say() posts to Telegram from tg.env, but with no tg.env/token/chat it returns 0 silently; no named reason is recorded or reported."],
  m_pj_planning: ["writePhaseBook confines planning writes to .agents/phases and .agents/planning marks, so the code tree is untouched. But there is no second planning address or way to move where planning is read."],
  m_pj_register: ["Core keeps a project register with per-host source paths. No separate planning-home address; Lane Pilot fixes planning at .agents/planning inside the tree."],
  m_pr_claude_pause: ["Pause probe has a helper run `sleep 40` and answer RESUMED in the same turn. Missing: stopping the process tree, confirmed exit, resume by session id."],
  m_pr_codex_pause: ["Same generic pause probe for every provider: a long command and a one-word answer. No stop, no confirmed exit, no resume by thread."],
  m_pr_codex_probe: ["Probe runs as the pm-reader role through fullAccessSpawn, with the prompt saying not to write. No sandbox enforces a write-only-own-file root, and nothing checks what it wrote."],
  m_pr_design_eval: ["compareDesigns scores two pages with a code rubric from browser measurements. No independent judge model, no pictures, no grounds. Driven by scripts/lp-design-eval.ts only."],
  m_pr_doc_drill: ["Documentary probe is a prompt whose answer must contain LISTED; judged by the answer text only. No check of traces of the real session (no tool or write trace), not claude-specific."],
  m_rd_accounts: ["windowHold only decides if a machine's window is closed (>=98%). Per-host window read exists (cockpit_windows) but no list with one entry per subscription plus its machine."],
  m_restart_scoped: ["Seat counts (ops.pool_size, ops.verify_pool_size) are frozen per run and apply only to new runs. Turn ceiling, lease expiry and attempt lifetime are read live; no restart-only class."],
  m_sd_answer: ["The drill covers a writer that asks a question (NEEDS_HUMAN, no file, not accepted). It does not test that edit-free work closes on an answer receipt the first time while code work does not."],
  m_sd_approve: ["live_word covers the green path only: a task waits for the owner's word and lands after task_word RPC yes. No red-branch refusal, and the word comes by RPC, not a real Approve press."],
  m_sd_lift: ["Lift is exercised only dry: a dry lift event is recorded, and a lift with a live door does nothing. It never runs the real lift or checks that the log holds the pid and wrapper lines."],
  m_sd_merge: ["The drill enters from the terminal (dispatch-bb) and proves the single merge path under a same-line conflict. No separate command-line merge verb drill; bb lane-pilot revert is not drilled."],
  m_sd_outage: ["Dry run (LP_WATCH_DRY=1) against a door that never answers: it records an outage and a dry lift. No real daemon is killed, no real lift or return, no check of the two Telegram messages."],
  m_sd_skills: ["Drill checks a skill named on a task reaches the writer's thread. No window, door and disk check of a skills screen, no emptiness explanation, no file-survives-press check."],
  m_sh_publish: ["deliberate: the ship workflow pushes and opens the pull request itself — the owner ordered releases without asking (2026-11-01); the card leaves the push to a person"],
  m_sp_install_watch: ["No-admin install exists (user systemd unit, else crontab @reboot; Windows task and shell:startup only in the doc). Missing: a refusal of the scheduler task named in words before falling back; sudo -n failure is silent."],
  m_sp_smoke_mac: ["A single launchctl list grep after install. No list of verbs and host prerequisites, and the exit code is not a count of failures."],
